{"tool_name":"strong","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"strong","home":"https://github.com/chrisquince/STRONG","license":"MIT","summary":"STRONG resolves strains on assembly graphs by resolving variants on core COGs using co-occurrence across multiple samples.","addition_date":"2021-11-17T20:55:26.806942Z","last_update_date":"2021-11-17T20:55:26.809495Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:strong","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"christopher.quince@earlham.ac.uk","name":"Christopher Quince","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1884-8440","typeEntity":"Person"},{"email":"sergey.nurk@nih.gov","name":"Sergey Nurk","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Coding region prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0436"},{"term":"Haplotype mapping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0487"},{"term":"Sequence assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0310"}]}],"name":"STRONG","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Jennifer","publication":[{"doi":"10.1186/S13059-021-02419-7","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2021, The Author(s).We introduce STrain Resolution ON assembly Graphs (STRONG), which identifies strains de novo, from multiple metagenome samples. STRONG performs coassembly, and binning into metagenome assembled genomes (MAGs), and stores the coassembly graph prior to variant simplification. This enables the subgraphs and their unitig per-sample coverages, for individual single-copy core genes (SCGs) in each MAG, to be extracted. A Bayesian algorithm, BayesPaths, determines the number of strains present, their haplotypes or sequences on the SCGs, and abundances. STRONG is validated using synthetic communities and for a real anaerobic digestor time series generates haplotypes that match those observed from long Nanopore reads.","authors":[{"name":"Chikhi R."},{"name":